NAME
    shell - start the managed interactive shell environment

SYNOPSIS
    shell [<shell-argument> ...]

DESCRIPTION
    shell starts the program named by SHELL, integrating it with m-managed shell
    configuration and state.

    bash is started with the managed bash rcfile.
    zsh receives managed startup files through a user-state ZDOTDIR.
    sh, dash and ash receive the managed ENV file.
    Other shells are executed without a shell-specific configuration adapter.

    Arguments are forwarded to the selected shell.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m shell [arguments].

    SHELL
        Shell executable to start. Defaults to sh when unset or empty.
    m_SHELL_EXT
        Exported shell-extension value used by managed shell configuration.

EXIT STATUS
    On success shell replaces itself with the selected shell.
    Non-zero status indicates state/configuration preparation or exec failure.
